  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining linguistic diversity and multilingualism in Mekong  countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contributing to UNESCO&#x2019;s role as the lead agency for the UN-wide implementation of the International Decade of Indigenous Languages 2022-2032 and in line with the approved 41 C/5 programme&#x2019;s outcome 5 to enhance the protection and promotion of the diversity of heritage and cultural expressions, CI Unit at UNESCO Bangkok proposes multi-stakeholder activities, including consultations with Indigenous civil society organizations and Member States to support the use and preservation of Indigenous languages in the Mekong countries. In addition, the proposed activities will aim to support the development of open solutions for increased use of Indigenous languages in public domains, including in the media.</narrative>
  </description>
